---
title: Tooling — Knowledge Islands
description: "Start using Knowledge Islands tooling: install the ki CLI, work with compatible harnesses, and govern a repository with source-labelled guidance."
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{% from "macros/icons.njk" import kiIcon %}

<section class="section-navy hero-section hero-section-standard">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <p class="overline-gold">Practical tooling</p>
    <h1 class="heading-display-light" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3.25rem); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; max-width: 22ch;">A clear path from install to governed work.</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: rgb(245 239 224 / 75%); max-width: 56ch; line-height: 1.7;">The public guide to the released <code>ki</code> command, compatible harnesses, and the workflows they enable. This site explains the journey; the owning repositories remain the source for executable behaviour and reusable capabilities.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-parchment section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <p class="overline">Released tools</p>
      <h2>Every tool has the same two routes.</h2>
      <p>Each released command-line tool has a page at <code>/tooling/&lt;tool&gt;/</code> and a stable installer endpoint at <code>/install/&lt;tool&gt;</code>. Both are generated from one website-owned registry, so a tool's page, its endpoint and the version it advertises always move together. The owning repository still decides what is released.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3col" style="gap: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
{%- for tool in tools %}
      <a href="/tooling/{{ tool.slug }}/" class="card-ki tool-card" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="symbol-circle symbol-circle-{{ tool.accent }}">{{ kiIcon(tool.icon, 22) }}</div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.625rem;"><code>{{ tool.name }}</code></h2>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; margin: 0;">{{ tool.tagline }}</p>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; margin: 0.625rem 0 0;">{{ tool.version }} · {{ tool.maturity }}</p>
      </a>
{%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <p class="overline">Start here</p>
      <h2>Choose the task in front of you.</h2>
      <p>Install the CLI once, bootstrap your user environment, then activate only the skills and harnesses your work needs. Each page below names its source so you can move to the owner when a command, release, or capability needs exact detail.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2col" style="gap: 1.5rem;">
      <a href="/tooling/harnesses/" class="card-ki tool-card" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="symbol-circle symbol-circle-teal">{{ kiIcon("archipelago", 22) }}</div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.625rem;">Use compatible harnesses</h2>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; margin: 0;">Understand the canonical harness, inspect compatible additions, and activate capabilities in the right scope.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/tooling/guidance/" class="card-ki tool-card" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="symbol-circle symbol-circle-forest">{{ kiIcon("compass", 22) }}</div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.625rem;">Govern a repository</h2>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; margin: 0;">Bootstrap an environment, add skills deliberately, and use native repository operations safely.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-mist section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none;">
      <p class="overline">Ownership boundary</p>
      <h2>This is a guide, not a second command reference.</h2>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/knowledgeislands/tools-ki">tools-ki</a> owns the released CLI, its installer, command help, and release artefacts. The <a href="https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agentic-harness">KI Agentic Harness</a> owns reusable skills and other agentic capabilities. <a href="/specifications/">KI Specifications</a> owns portable normative contracts. Use the source links on each page when precision or the latest state matters.</p>
      <p>The tools above are one part of a wider ecosystem. <a href="/projects/">Projects</a> lists every public repository — the principal knowledge bases, the harness, the specifications, the MCP servers, and the delivery infrastructure — and says what each one is the authority for.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
